  "limitations": [
    "API-09 owns the process-wide application/problem+json vocabulary, correlation middleware, and global status and terminal-error normalization. API-08 adds strict validation seams and fixed non-reflective route-local failures, but does not claim that global response contract.",
    "DEL-05 owns default runnable API, worker, repository, deterministic LLM, and connector composition. API-08 proves the schema boundaries through installed routes and injected real services, adapters, and repositories; it does not claim the default process wires every runtime dependency.",
    "DEL-07 owns the committed OpenAPI snapshot, generated TypeScript client, and drift gate. API-08 preserves typed FastAPI/Pydantic contracts and runs existing live-schema regressions but does not claim generated client artifacts.",
    "RuntimeInputContract computes a canonical request-schema hash, but the persisted controlled-READ operation currently seals only the request schema ID, not that hash. The executor validates against the adapter-declared schema before reservation, yet cannot independently detect a same-ID changed request schema without a later persisted request-schema hash.",
    "The controlled executor validates output against the hash-bound schema before artifact construction and records output schema identity, version, and hash in provenance. The artifact repository does not receive a schema resolver and therefore cannot independently revalidate an artifact body against that schema during add or hydration.",
    "Webhook authentication intentionally remains signature-first over exact raw bytes. Its bounded transport, strict source mapper, resolved input-schema validation, and safe pointer behavior are the separately proven API-05 seam included in this regression gate; API-08 does not insert the shared JSON parser ahead of signature verification.",
    "The central runtime policy supports local-only $ref and $dynamicRef inside one schema document and rejects remote references. Draft 2020-12 does not implement the legacy $recursiveRef/$recursiveAnchor vocabulary, so actual subschemas containing those keywords fail closed; annotation/default data remains inert. Catalog multi-file resolution is a separate boundary.",
    "The real-provider tests use injected delegates and no network, and connector tests use deterministic local gateways. No live model provider, external connector, remote schema, or network fallback is exercised or claimed."
  ]
